# CRM PROJECT - CORE STANDARDS

## Locked technology stack (from the SRS - NEVER change)
- Backend: Laravel (PHP). Frontend: HTML rendered with Blade templates + CSS + vanilla JavaScript.
- Database: MySQL (InnoDB, utf8mb4).
- FORBIDDEN unless both developers and the SRS owner approve in writing: Vue, Inertia, React, Livewire,
  TypeScript, PostgreSQL/SQLite-only features, any SPA framework.
- Allowed tooling: Laravel's default Vite pipeline, Composer/npm packages that do NOT replace the stack
  (e.g. Chart.js for charts, FullCalendar for the calendar, a PHP spreadsheet/PDF export library).
- Before adding ANY new package: state why, check it is maintained, and get the other developer's OK in the PR.

## Source of truth
- The SRS (CRM_Requirements_Specification.docx) wins over guesses. Follow it strictly.
- Reference requirement IDs (e.g. FR-LEAD-005, NFR-SEC-004) in code comments, tests, commits and PR titles.
- Priority order: P0 > P1 > P2. Never build P3 (Won't Have): native apps, workflow builder,
  AI insights, custom objects, integrations marketplace.
- If the SRS is ambiguous or you are tempted to deviate, STOP and ask; do not invent behaviour.

## Context first - no guesswork
- List the files you will read/modify before changing anything. Follow existing patterns.
- Never rewrite or reformat files outside the current task (two developers share this repo).
- Ask at most one clarifying question, and only when the SRS does not answer it.

## Challenge requests
- Point out edge cases (permissions, empty states, validation, concurrency) before coding.
- If a request conflicts with the SRS or the locked stack, say so and propose a compliant alternative.

## Quality
- Modular, testable code; small controllers; logic in Services/Actions; comments on non-obvious logic.
- Think beyond the file: migration + model + policy + request + controller + view + test are one feature.
- Every feature ships with: validation, authorization, audit fields, empty/error states, and tests.

## Two-developer collaboration
- Work only inside your owned module (see docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md). Shared files (layout, routes/web.php,
  navigation, base traits, config) are changed only in small, separate PRs that are merged fast.
- Never edit a migration that is already on `develop`; add a new one.
